---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
import salem from '../assets/salem.jpg';
---

<Base title="About" description="Who made this unofficial Spooky Bear 2026 guide, why it exists, and how to fix something that's wrong.">
  <article class="wrap about">
    <h1>About this site</h1>

    <div class="intro">
      <figure class="photo">
        <Image src={salem} alt="Salem on the Boatslip deck at sunset in camo shorts and a harness, holding a glowing star wand" width={520} widths={[320, 520, 760]} sizes="(max-width: 720px) 60vw, 260px" loading="eager" />
        <figcaption>Me, last Spooky Bear, tea dance at the Boatslip.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <strong>Hi, I’m Salem (he/him).</strong> I’m a frontend engineer and design-systems nerd who has spent 14+
          years making things for the web that are fast, accessible, and fun to use: component libraries used by
          thousands of developers, big design-system migrations, and plenty of small sites like this one. Before that
          I co-owned an escape room company, which is where I picked up the habit of wiring puzzles to
          microcontrollers and 3D-printing whatever didn’t exist yet.
        </p>
        <p>
          I live in Jamaica Plain with my partner and two cats, where a rotating cast of mad-scientist projects keeps
          me busy: a built-from-scratch CoreXY 3D printer, a wicked-smart apartment, and now this.
        </p>
        <p class="hiring">
          <strong>Hiring frontend engineers or architects?</strong> I’m currently open to principal-level frontend and
          design-systems roles. Have a look at <a href="https://salemghoweri.com/" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">salemghoweri.com</a>,
          poke around <a href="https://github.com/sghoweri" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">my GitHub</a>, or just
          <a href="mailto:me@salemghoweri.com?subject=Hi%20from%20spookybear2026.com">say hi</a>. I’d love to talk.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why this exists</h2>
      <p>
        Spooky Bear is Ptown’s last big hurrah of the season, and every year the schedule is scattered across a dozen
        venue Instagrams, Facebook events and ticket pages. I wanted one mobile-friendly place to see everything,
        filter by day or venue, and star the stuff I don’t want to miss.
      </p>
      <p>
        It’s unofficial and run by one fan. It is not affiliated with
        <a href={SITE.organizer.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{SITE.organizer.name}</a>, who run the official
        Spooky Bear weekend, or with any venue listed here. If you want the official word, go to them.
      </p>

      <h2>How the data works</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Every event is a small text file in a <a href={SITE.repo} rel="noopener" target="_blank">public GitHub repo</a>, with a link back to wherever the details came from.</li>
        <li>Times, prices and lineups change at the last minute in Ptown. When we couldn’t confirm something, the event says so instead of guessing.</li>
        <li>“My den” favourites are stored only in your browser. There are no accounts and nothing is sent anywhere.</li>
        <li>The site uses the most basic analytics and error monitoring so I know it works. Details on the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Spotted a mistake? Missing an event?</h2>
      <p>
        Tell me and I’ll fix it, usually the same day during the weekend. Flyers, Instagram links and screenshots all
        help. No GitHub account needed.
      </p>
      <p class="cta">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" data-feedback="wrong">Report wrong info</button>
        <button class="btn btn-secondary" type="button" data-feedback="event">Suggest an event</button>
        <button class="btn btn-ghost" type="button" data-feedback="bug">Something’s broken</button>
      </p>
      <p class="small">Prefer GitHub? <a href={`${SITE.repo}/issues/new/choose`} rel="noopener" target="_blank">Open an issue directly</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-top: 24px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 3rem);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .intro {
    display: grid;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .photo {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 260px;
  }
  .photo :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    transform: rotate(-1.5deg);
  }
  .photo figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .hiring {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: rgba(255, 92, 154, 0.1);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 92, 154, 0.35);
  }
  .cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .small {
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .intro {
      grid-template-columns: 260px 1fr;
      align-items: start;
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }
</style>
